WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:18.259
As Aunt March's favorite grand-niece, Amy received many favors from her rich relative, including art lessons at the finest institute in town.

2
00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:23.023
On the first day of class, she realized that she already knew some of her classmates from school.

3
00:00:23.024 --> 00:00:29.189
These were the girls whose parents had the wealth to send their children to this particular place.

4
00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:35.532
"Amy? Amy March?" Christina cried disbelievingly on the first day of class.

5
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:43.382
"Christina! Mary! How lovely to see you again!" exclaimed Amy, genuinely pleased to see the girls,

6
00:00:43.383 --> 00:00:47.768
even though the memories of the limes incident still pricked her heart.

7
00:00:47.769 --> 00:00:52.488
Having survived many experiences, including almost losing a beloved sister,

8
00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:56.274
Amy felt life was too short to hold grudges.

9
00:00:56.275 --> 00:01:01.528
Instead, she chose to be friendly and kind even to those who had wronged her.

10
00:01:01.529 --> 00:01:09.147
Amy also tried her best to remain modest, even though Mrs. Meade, the art instructor, often showered praise on Amy's talent.

11
00:01:09.147 --> 00:01:15.343
"Lunch at my house this week, Amy," Mary informed her as the class was dismissed one afternoon.

12
00:01:15.343 --> 00:01:21.988
At some point during the classes, the girls had decided among themselves to take turns hosting a luncheon every Saturday.

13
00:01:21.988 --> 00:01:27.417
Amy had attended three so far, and it seemed to her that each girl tried to outshine the one before

14
00:01:27.418 --> 00:01:33.102
by preparing fancy feasts and desserts more suited for a ball than a midday meal.

15
00:01:33.103 --> 00:01:42.088
However, Amy doubted very much that the girls actually cooked the meals themselves; most likely they relied on servants to get the job done.

16
00:01:42.089 --> 00:01:48.356
After lunch, the girls would set out for some scenic place and spend the rest of the afternoon sketching, painting,

17
00:01:48.357 --> 00:01:51.827
and doing what all girls love best: gossiping.

18
00:01:51.828 --> 00:01:58.752
Amy knew that after Mary, it would be her turn to host a lunch and so began her worries.

19
00:01:58.753 --> 00:02:06.123
That evening, Amy drew up a schedule for her upcoming luncheon, including the menu and activities to follow the meal.

20
00:02:06.124 --> 00:02:10.738
She had checked her savings beforehand to make sure she had enough to finance the event.

21
00:02:10.739 --> 00:02:19.812
Fortunately, Amy received a generous salary from Aunt March, so she was able to put away a little extra each week for special occasions.

22
00:02:19.813 --> 00:02:26.801
Originally, Amy had wanted to save enough money to travel to Italy and paint to her heart's content.

23
00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:33.525
Sighing loudly, she said, disheartened, "Italy will have to wait till after lunch."

24
00:02:33.526 --> 00:02:41.035
Father, carrying a large basket of fresh, ripe vegetables, walked in as Amy was making her curious remark.

25
00:02:41.036 --> 00:02:48.615
Chuckling, he said, "I'm sure you know what you're talking about, but I haven't a clue what you mean."

26
00:02:48.616 --> 00:02:58.522
Slipping the paper into her pocket, Amy gave her father a hug and said, "It's nothing, Father, but I may ask for some of your vegetables next week."

27
00:02:58.523 --> 00:03:02.724
"As many as you like, darling," he replied, tweaking her nose.

28
00:03:02.725 --> 00:03:07.877
Amy spent a great deal of time (and money) making individual invitations for her lunch.

29
00:03:07.878 --> 00:03:12.735
Handing them out to the girls, Amy heard many compliments about her design and artwork.

30
00:03:12.736 --> 00:03:20.925
"I've hired a carriage that will take us to the most enchanting place in the world," she said as her old habit of bragging started to return.

31
00:03:20.926 --> 00:03:27.351
"I personally prefer oil paints but its beauty can be captured with any technique of your choice."

32
00:03:27.352 --> 00:03:34.526
On the eve of the party, Mother and Jo watched Amy anxiously as she scurried around like a little mouse preparing things.

33
00:03:34.527 --> 00:03:40.963
They waited for her instructions since Amy had asked for their help, along with that of Beth, Hannah, and Meg

34
00:03:40.964 --> 00:03:45.958
(who had to decline because her husband's friends were coming for dinner that very day).

35
00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:50.736
"Do you know how much she's spent so far?" Jo asked disapprovingly.

36
00:03:50.737 --> 00:03:54.740
"It's her money. She can do as she likes," Mother replied.

37
00:03:54.741 --> 00:04:04.122
"But she's blowing her hard-earned money on just this one day and for a bunch of whiny girls who don't even care about her," Jo said critically.

38
00:04:04.123 --> 00:04:12.301
"Jo, even though we may not agree with Amy's idea, we have agreed to help her, so let's keep our word," Mother said.

39
00:04:12.301 --> 00:04:20.081
It was not easy to do even that, as Jo discovered, with Amy's short temper, sharp reproofs, and constant corrections.

40
00:04:20.082 --> 00:04:28.304
"Jo, I said beat the eggs one at a time, not all together!" Amy shouted after she had asked her sister to help bake a cake.

41
00:04:28.305 --> 00:04:34.922
"Jo, don't slice the meat so thickly!" she corrected after asking Jo to help with the sandwich meat.

42
00:04:34.923 --> 00:04:48.526
"Jo, must you sing while you wash the vegetables? It's rather annoying!" she snapped when Jo started to hum aloud to entertain herself.

43
00:04:48.527 --> 00:04:55.156
"It's you who's annoying," Jo wanted to yell back, but she bit her lip and did as Amy asked.

44
00:04:55.157 --> 00:05:00.629
Everyone fell into bed exhausted that night, looking forward to a restful sleep.

45
00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:04.609
But a few hours later at the crack of dawn, Amy woke them up.

46
00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:12.374
After a poor attempt at an apology, Amy said to her sisters, "This house must sparkle and shine before the girls come."

47
00:05:12.375 --> 00:05:19.897
The two sisters, yawning and rubbing their eyes, glanced over at the clock, which read 6:15 a.m.

48
00:05:19.898 --> 00:05:24.956
Groaning loudly, Jo murmured some unpleasant things about her youngest sister.

49
00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:29.703
Unfortunately for Amy the weather did not cooperate with her plans.

50
00:05:29.704 --> 00:05:34.348
It was pouring cats and dogs while low thunder rumbled in the distance.

51
00:05:34.349 --> 00:05:41.113
Looking outside, Mother said, "Perhaps Mr. Laurence will allow you girls to paint in his conservatory."

52
00:05:41.114 --> 00:05:49.108
"The rain may let up yet," Amy said hopefully, "so Father should still go and collect the horse and carriage anyway."

53
00:05:49.109 --> 00:05:55.799
Ever the gentleman, Father put on his hat, found his umbrella, and set out to do as his daughter requested.

54
00:05:55.799 --> 00:06:02.609
Jo and Beth got to work cleaning every inch of the house, while Mother and Hannah finished preparing the meal.

55
00:06:02.609 --> 00:06:09.250
By the time they got everything ready, the March home looked quite presentable for a group of upper-class girls.

56
00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:15.810
"Now I'm going upstairs to change so if anyone comes while I'm gone, please make them feel welcome,"

57
00:06:15.811 --> 00:06:20.429
Amy said to her sisters while she went to make herself beautiful.

58
00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:28.558
Around noon, when the guests were scheduled to come, Amy, looking very pretty in a green dress, stood waiting by the door like a good hostess.

59
00:06:28.559 --> 00:06:33.073
At the sounds of a carriage approaching, Amy excitedly opened the door.

60
00:06:33.074 --> 00:06:41.852
She discovered it was only Father returning, not with a grand carriage, but with an open wagon being pulled by an old, smelly horse.

61
00:06:41.853 --> 00:06:47.770
Running outside into the rain, Amy cried, "Father! This isn't the one I hired!"

62
00:06:47.771 --> 00:06:56.267
Trying to calm his daughter down, Father explained, "Mr. Glendale didn't want his finest horse and carriage out in the terrible weather.

63
00:06:56.268 --> 00:06:59.234
He'll give you a discount for these."

64
00:06:59.235 --> 00:07:06.269
Amy's neatly brushed and styled hair was soon dripping wet and her clothes clung to her like a second skin.

65
00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:13.797
"Amy, you must change out of those clothes or you'll catch a cold," Mother said, pushing her upstairs to her room.

66
00:07:13.798 --> 00:07:18.935
Sniffing, Amy argued, "But this is my best dress.

67
00:07:18.936 --> 00:07:21.635
I don't have anything else to wear."

68
00:07:21.636 --> 00:07:29.335
"Don't exaggerate," Mother said firmly. "You have a closet full of pretty things. Now go and change!"

69
00:07:29.336 --> 00:07:38.929
Shuffling her feet, Amy cried, "Can the day get any worse?" It did for poor Amy.
